effectively zero. Palma North carries $39,905 of recurring concessions incl. one unit at 3 months free. Stabilized assets here should sit near zero; see lease-up overrides below."},"Loss to Lease %":{"group":"Revenue Metrics","how":"(Market rent \u2212 in-place rent) / market rent, current rent roll","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"\u2264 5.0%","in_range":"5.0% \u2013 10.0%","below":"> 10.0%","green_cutoff":0.05,"red_cutoff":0.1,"basis":"The Landing T12 loss-to-lease was $2,629,358 on $16,489,513 market rent potential = 15.9%, which scores red against this band. Before wiring it, confirm Yardi 'Market rent potential' is set to true achievable market rent \u2014 if it is aspirational, every property will read artificially high."},"NOI Margin %":{"group":"Expense Metrics","how":"NOI / total revenue, T12 accrual basis (GL 5999-9999 / 4999-9999)","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 68.0%","in_range":"62.0% \u2013 67.9%","below":"< 62.0%","green_cutoff":0.68,"red_cutoff":0.62,"basis":"Band set by Kaelin, July 2026, superseding the data-derived range. Aggressive relative to current performance: The Landing T12 NOI of $9,354,210 on revenue $14,077,351 = 66.4%, which now scores amber. Typical stabilized multifamily runs 55\u201362%, so the red line sits at the top of the national norm \u2014 justified by this portfolio's Prop 13 tax basis and low utility load ($745/unit vs. $1,870 SF benchmark)."},"Budget Variance %":{"group":"Expense Metrics","how":"ABS( (actual controllable opex \u2212 budget) / budget ), YTD \u2014 absolute magnitude, direction ignored","direction":"Lower is better (abs)","exceeding":"< 5.0%","in_range":"5.0% \u2013 10.0%","below":"> 10.0%","green_cutoff":0.05,"red_cutoff":0.1,"basis":"Band set by Kaelin, July 2026. Scored on absolute magnitude, so a 12% underspend flags red exactly like a 12% overrun \u2014 correct, because a large favorable variance is usually timing lag or deferred maintenance rather than outperformance. This removes the need for two-sided handling on this KPI. Boundary: the \u2264/> classifier puts exactly 5.0% in green and exactly 10.0% in amber; only matters at the precise boundary."},"Controllable OpEx/Unit":{"group":"Expense Metrics","how":"Controllable opex (utilities, contract services, R&M, payroll, G&A, marketing, turnover) / unit count, T12 annualized. Excludes taxes, insurance, management fee","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"\u2264 $7,200","in_range":"$7,200 \u2013 $8,600","below":"> $8,600","green_cutoff":7200,"red_cutoff":8600,"basis":"The Landing T12 actual = $7,784/unit ($649/mo) across 263 units. Sum of the SF-adjusted category benchmarks = $8,050/unit. Band brackets both, so the current actual scores in-range."},"# of Tours/Leads/Applications":{"group":"Lease-up Status","how":"Tours / available units, per month. NORMALIZE \u2014 raw counts are not comparable across a 263-unit and a 46-unit asset","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 3.0 per avail. unit/mo","in_range":"1.5 \u2013 2.9","below":"< 1.5","green_cutoff":3,"red_cutoff":1.5,"basis":"Palma North logged 28 shows over 05/01\u201307/14/26 against 22 available units \u2248 0.6/unit/mo; Palma South logged 21. The raw counts on the current scorecard cannot be compared property to property \u2014 normalizing is the fix."},"Closing Ratio":{"group":"Lease-up Status","how":"Signed leases / tours, trailing 3 months","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 30.0%","in_range":"20.0% \u2013 29.9%","below":"< 20.0%","green_cutoff":0.3,"red_cutoff":0.2,"basis":"Palma South: 4 applications on 21 shows = 19.0% applied, 3 approved = 14.3%. Industry stabilized norm is 25\u201335%; luxury urban product runs at the low end of that."},"# of Renewals":{"group":"Lease-up Status","how":"Renewals signed / lease expirations in the period (renewal conversion rate)","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 60.0%","in_range":"45.0% \u2013 59.9%","below":"< 45.0%","green_cutoff":0.6,"red_cutoff":0.45,"basis":"Normalized from a raw count. 50\u201360% is the typical stabilized range. Always read alongside % Increase so retention isn't being bought with flat renewals."},"# of offers that are 30 days":{"group":"Lease-up Status","how":"Renewal offers issued \u2265 30 days before expiration / total upcoming expirations (on-time issuance rate)","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 95.0%","in_range":"85.0% \u2013 94.9%","below":"< 85.0%","green_cutoff":0.95,"red_cutoff":0.85,"basis":"DEFINITION AMBIGUOUS on the current sheet. Read the other way \u2014 offers left outstanding 30+ days \u2014 lower is better and the band flips to green \u2264 5%, amber 5\u201315%, red > 15%. Confirm intent before wiring."},"# of accepted/pending offers":{"group":"Lease-up Status","how":"Accepted offers / offers issued, trailing 3 months. Track 'pending' separately as an aging, not as a score","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 55.0%","in_range":"40.0% \u2013 54.9%","below":"< 40.0%","green_cutoff":0.55,"red_cutoff":0.4,"basis":"Follows from the 60% renewal-conversion green: acceptance rate should sit slightly below conversion once non-responses are netted out."},"# of month to month":{"group":"Lease-up Status","how":"MTM leases / occupied units, at month-end","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"\u2264 2.0%","in_range":"2.0% \u2013 5.0%","below":"> 5.0%","green_cutoff":0.02,"red_cutoff":0.05,"basis":"The Landing earned $68,774 of MTM fee income in T12 \u2014 MTM is revenue-positive short term but a forecasting and turnover risk. Palma North reported 0 MTM leases at 07/14/26."},"% Increase":{"group":"Lease-up Status","how":"Average renewal rent increase %, trailing 3 months","direction":"Band (two-sided)","exceeding":"+4.0% \u2013 +7.0%","in_range":"+1.0% \u2013 +3.9%, or > +7.0%","below":"< +1.0%","green_cutoff":0.04,"red_cutoff":0.01,"basis":"TWO-SIDED: above +7% the green flips to amber, because aggressive renewals push turnover and re-lease cost that exceeds the rent gain. Anchored to SF rent growth of ~5.7\u20135.9% YoY."},"Total Deliquency":{"group":"AR/AP Metrics","how":"Total gross resident AR balance / one month's billed rent, at month-end","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"\u2264 1.0%","in_range":"1.0% \u2013 3.0%","below":"> 3.0%","green_cutoff":0.01,"red_cutoff":0.03,"basis":"The Landing T12 net bad debt was $100,867 on $14.08M revenue = 0.7%. Score on GROSS AR: Palma North's rent roll nets to a \u2212$84,450 credit balance because of two large prepaid accounts, which would hide real delinquency behind a negative total."},"Split Between 30/60/90":{"group":"AR/AP Metrics","how":"Share of total AR aged 60+ days","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"\u2264 15.0%","in_range":"15.0% \u2013 30.0%","below":"> 30.0%","green_cutoff":0.15,"red_cutoff":0.3,"basis":"A distribution cannot be scored as a single value. Collapsing it to the 60+ share keeps the signal that matters (older AR is materially less collectible) while still fitting the three-band key."},"POs over 30 days":{"group":"AR/AP Metrics","how":"Open POs aged > 30 days / total open POs","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"\u2264 10.0%","in_range":"10.0% \u2013 20.0%","below":"> 20.0%","green_cutoff":0.1,"red_cutoff":0.2,"basis":"Suggested operating standard \u2014 no portfolio history for this metric exists in the source files. Recalibrate after one quarter of actuals."},"# of invoices processed":{"group":"AR/AP Metrics","how":"Invoices approved within 5 business days / invoices received","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 95.0%","in_range":"85.0% \u2013 94.9%","below":"< 85.0%","green_cutoff":0.95,"red_cutoff":0.85,"basis":"Reframed from a raw count to a cycle-time rate. A high invoice count is neither good nor bad on its own \u2014 it measures workload, not performance."},"# of work orders":{"group":"Maintenance Metrics","how":"Count of work orders still open in the queue at time of reporting (point-in-time backlog, not volume opened)","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"< 5","in_range":"5 \u2013 9","below":"\u2265 10","green_cutoff":4,"red_cutoff":9,"basis":"Band set by Kaelin, July 2026. Measures backlog rather than volume, so an absolute count holds across asset sizes \u2014 a clean queue is a clean queue at 263 units or 46. Boundary note: 10 fell in both the amber and red bands as specified and is scored red, making amber 5\u20139. Cutoffs are integers (green \u2264 4 = under 5; red > 9 = 10 or more)."},"Work orders over two days":{"group":"Maintenance Metrics","how":"Count of open work orders aged more than 48 hours, at time of reporting","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"0","in_range":"1 \u2013 2","below":"\u2265 3","green_cutoff":0,"red_cutoff":2,"basis":"Band set by Kaelin, July 2026. Zero-tolerance green \u2014 a single ticket past 48 hours moves the property off green. NOTE: this KPI exists on 'KPI (Flipped Axis)' but is missing from 'Nicholas MVP' \u2014 the two tabs carry 20 and 19 KPIs respectively."},"Online Review Rating":{"group":"Resident Experience","how":"Average Google / ILS star rating, trailing 90 days","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 4.50","in_range":"4.00 \u2013 4.49","below":"< 4.00","green_cutoff":4.5,"red_cutoff":4,"basis":"PROPOSED \u2014 no portfolio history in the source files. 4.5+ is the practical threshold at which rating stops suppressing ILS conversion; below 4.0 it actively costs tours."},"Review Response Rate":{"group":"Resident Experience","how":"Reviews responded to within 5 business days / total reviews received","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 95.0%","in_range":"80.0% \u2013 94.9%","below":"< 80.0%","green_cutoff":0.95,"red_cutoff":0.8,"basis":"PROPOSED. Response rate is fully within onsite control, unlike the rating itself, so the green bar is set high deliberately."},"Resident Satisfaction (CSAT)":{"group":"Resident Experience","how":"Satisfied + very satisfied responses / total responses, annual resident survey","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 85.0%","in_range":"70.0% \u2013 84.9%","below":"< 70.0%","green_cutoff":0.85,"red_cutoff":0.7,"basis":"PROPOSED. Report alongside response count \u2014 a 90% CSAT on 8 responses at a 263-unit asset is not a signal. Suppress the rating below ~30 responses."},"Maintenance Satisfaction":{"group":"Resident Experience","how":"Satisfied responses / completed work-order surveys returned, trailing 90 days","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 90.0%","in_range":"75.0% \u2013 89.9%","below":"< 75.0%","green_cutoff":0.9,"red_cutoff":0.75,"basis":"PROPOSED. Pairs with the two maintenance KPIs: closing tickets fast at low satisfaction means work is being marked complete before it is."},"Open Elise Tasks":{"group":"Open EliseAI Tasks","how":"Count of unresolved tasks in the EliseAI queue at time of reporting","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"< 5","in_range":"5 \u2013 9","below":"\u2265 10","green_cutoff":4,"red_cutoff":9,"basis":"PROPOSED, mirroring the open work order band set 07/2026 \u2014 both are point-in-time queue backlogs, so holding one convention across them keeps the scorecard readable. Integer cutoffs (green \u2264 4; red > 9)."},"Elise Tasks over 24 Hours":{"group":"Open EliseAI Tasks","how":"Count of open EliseAI tasks aged more than 24 hours","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"0","in_range":"1 \u2013 2","below":"\u2265 3","green_cutoff":0,"red_cutoff":2,"basis":"PROPOSED, mirroring the 'Work orders over two days' band. Tighter clock than maintenance (24h vs 48h) because these are mostly prospect and resident replies, where response speed drives conversion."},"AI Containment Rate":{"group":"Open EliseAI Tasks","how":"Prospect conversations resolved by EliseAI with no human handoff / total conversations","direction":"Higher is better","exceeding":"\u2265 80.0%","in_range":"65.0% \u2013 79.9%","below":"< 65.0%","green_cutoff":0.8,"red_cutoff":0.65,"basis":"PROPOSED. Read against Closing Ratio, not alone \u2014 high containment with a falling close rate means the AI is deflecting leads rather than converting them."},"Avg First Response Time":{"group":"Open EliseAI Tasks","how":"Mean minutes from new prospect inquiry to first reply (AI or human)","direction":"Lower is better","exceeding":"\u2264 5 min","in_range":"5 \u2013 15 min","below":"> 15 min","green_cutoff":5,"red_cutoff":15,"basis":"PROPOSED. Minutes, not hours \u2014 an AI leasing assistant should make this near-instant, so a reading above 15 minutes usually indicates a routing or integration failure rather than slow staff."}},"leaseup_overrides":[{"kpi":"Leased %","approach":"Score net absorption instead","exceeding":"\u2265 6 net leases/mo per 100 units","in_range":"3 \u2013 5.9","below":"< 3"},{"kpi":"Concession Load %","approach":"Widen \u2014 concessions are the lease-up tool","exceeding":"\u2264 4.0%","in_range":"4.0% \u2013 8.0%","below":"> 8.0%"},{"kpi":"NOI Margin %","approach":"Score vs. lease-up pro forma NOI, not a margin %","exceeding":"\u2265 pro forma","in_range":"within \u221210% of pro forma","below":"worse than \u221210%"},{"kpi":"Controllable OpEx/Unit","approach":"Score vs. budget, not the per-unit benchmark","exceeding":"\u2264 budget \u22122%","in_range":"budget \u22122% to +3%","below":"> budget +3%"}],"measured":{"the-landing":{"source":"workbook Source Delinquency tab, via docs/landing.json","as_of":"2026-07-20","kpis":["Split Between 30/60/90","Total Deliquency"]}}}